  "answer": "## What “Respect `LinkComponent`” means in `ListItemButton`\n\n`ListItemButton` is an overridable component whose element type and props are controlled through its type map and `component`/`LinkComponent`-style integration.\n\nFrom the Joy props/types, the key customization mechanism is that `ListItemButton` is **polymorphic**: its rendered element is determined by the `component` prop (and the default is `div`). This is expressed in the generic type map and props:\n\n- `ListItemButtonTypeMap` defaults `D` to `'div'` (so by default it renders a `div`) (packages/mui-joy/src/ListItemButton/ListItemButtonProps.ts).\n- `ListItemButtonProps` uses `OverrideProps<..., D>` and includes `component?: React.ElementType` (packages/mui-joy/src/ListItemButton/ListItemButtonProps.ts).\n- The only slot is `'root'` (packages/mui-joy/src/ListItemButton/ListItemButtonProps.ts).\n\n### Relevant type definitions\n```ts\nexport type ListItemButtonProps<\n  D extends React.ElementType = ListItemButtonTypeMap['defaultComponent'],\n  P = { component?: React.ElementType },\n> = OverrideProps<ListItemButtonTypeMap<P, D>, D>;\n```\n(packages/mui-joy/src/ListItemButton/ListItemButtonProps.ts)\n\n## How this connects to `LinkComponent`\n\nWhile the excerpts you provided include **only the props/types file**, the architecture implies the fix you’re asking about (“Respect `LinkComponent`”) would be implemented by ensuring that when a caller supplies a link-like component (typically via a prop named `LinkComponent` in the higher-level API, e.g., a menu/list item integration), `ListItemButton` passes that through to the actual rendered element—i.e., it should end up as the `component`/element type rather than being ignored.\n\nConcretely, the expectation is: **the component used for the rendered root should be the provided link component**, leveraging the polymorphic `component` mechanism defined in `ListItemButtonProps` (packages/mui-joy/src/ListItemButton/ListItemButtonProps.ts).",
